      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Wire Gauge Conversion Guide\n\n**Common Wire Gauges:**\n- **Household copper wiring**: AWG 12 or 14\n- **Telephone wire**: AWG 22, 24, or 26\n- **Power transmission**: AWG 0000 to 2\n\n**Conversion Tips:**\n- 1 inch = 25.4 mm\n- To find cross-sectional area: A = π × (d/2)²\n- Resistance decreases as wire diameter increases\n- Ampacity increases with larger cross-sectional area"
